.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="Pauling&#x27;s first rule (1929): each cation is surrounded by a polyhedron of anions whose size is fixed by the radius ratio r_+/r_-. A polyhedron is stable only while the anions still touch the cation, which sets the limits \sqrt2-1=0.414 (octahedral), \sqrt3-1=0.732 (cubic), and so on. radius_ratio_coordination applies the rule; here it is tested against observed structures.">

